# English translations of the interface.
#
# The source language is German. Every msgid is thus the German sentence as
# it stands in the code or the template. Whoever changes something there
# changes the key with it: 'makemessages -l en' then shows the place as new,
# and the old entry slips to the end of the file. The English terms follow
# the entries that are there: 'Haus' is "site", 'Ware' "product".
#
# Whoever adds something compiles the messages again afterwards (see DEPLOYMENT.md).
